Phase 3.1 Lifecycle Verification Report
=======================================

TESTS COVERING TASK LIFECYCLE
-----------------------------
1. test_successful_execution_records_one_completed_attempt
   - Verifies handle -> COMPLETED -> one attempt recorded
   - operation_id starts with "op_", attempt_number == 1

2. test_retry_preserves_task_id_and_history
   - Verifies retry of FAILED task creates second attempt
   - attempts[0] == FAILED, attempts[1] == COMPLETED
   - task_id preserved, errors carried forward

3. test_retry_is_refused_for_unmarked_capability
   - Verifies retry refused for non-retry-safe capability (jarvis.web_search)
   - requires_user_decision = True
   - attempt count unchanged

4. test_retry_of_terminal_task_is_rejected
   - Verifies retry of COMPLETED task raises AjError

5. test_cancel_moves_non_terminal_task_to_cancelled
   - Verifies cancel_task moves non-terminal task to CANCELLED
   - aj.cancel() returns False (already cancelled)

6. test_cancel_of_terminal_task_changes_nothing
   - Verifies cancel of COMPLETED task is rejected
   - Task status stays COMPLETED

7. test_cancel_while_executing_requests_without_claiming_stop
   - Verifies EXECUTING -> CANCEL_REQUESTED with "not interrupted" message
   - Persisted request can be confirmed by operator -> CANCELLED

8. test_attempt_model_survives_reload
   - Verifies _start_attempt/_finish_attempt survive config reload
   - operation_id and attempt_id persisted correctly

CANCELLATION SEMANTICS VERIFIED
--------------------------------
- Non-running states (RECEIVED, UNDERSTANDING, PLANNED, AUTHORIZED,
  FAILED) -> CANCELLED immediately
- EXECUTING -> CANCEL_REQUESTED (honest: "not interrupted")
- Terminal tasks (COMPLETED) -> cancel refused, status unchanged
- Cooperative cancellation: no forced termination of running work

RETRY SEMANTICS VERIFIED
-------------------------
- retry_safe default False per capability
- Only aj.echo and aj.health_check have retry_safe=True
- Unmarked capabilities: retry refused, requires_user_decision=True
- Attempts history preserved: first attempt stays FAILED, second is new
- Retry budget exhaustion -> RECOVERING -> ESCALATED -> requires_user_decision

EXIT CODES VERIFIED
-------------------
- EXIT_OK (0): successful operations
- EXIT_UNSAFE (6): retry of non-retry-safe capability
- EXIT_CONFIG (5): invalid configuration
- EXIT_NOT_FOUND (1): task/not found
- EXIT_FAILURE (2): operation refused (terminal task, retry refused)
- EXIT_CANCELLED (4): task was cancelled
- EXIT_RECOVERY_REQUIRED (3): capability not replay-safe